		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-05T05:20:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize Cocoon and Wind submodules\n\nUpdate the Cocoon extension host submodule to include regenerated build artifacts following the decomposition of the `Window/Namespace` module into dedicated factory modules (OutputChannel, StatusBar, Terminal, Webview). This ensures the `Target/` directory aligns with the new PascalCase directory hierarchy and updated import paths.\n\nSimultaneously, update the Wind UI service submodule to bump the `CommandCatalogVersion` and `ServiceCatalogVersion` constants in the generated effect files. This synchronization maintains consistency between the runtime service registry and the latest upstream state without altering the API surface (544 commands, 483 services).\n\nThese updates ensure build stability across the extension host and UI layers while adhering to the project's modular architecture and naming conventions.",
			"SHA": "bf890ddfe7a9daa4f581c53e36eb8a2b169e8b7f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-05T05:12:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize SideCar and Sky submodules for bridge modularization\n\nUpdate the SideCar and Sky submodules to their latest states to integrate the final stages of the UI bridge architecture refactoring.\n\n**Sky Changes**: Decompose the monolithic `Bridge.ts` into dedicated installer modules (`InstallDebug`, `InstallTasksAndDecorations`). This isolates logic for debug lifecycle, custom editors, workspace edits, and batched UI decorations. The new modular structure utilizes dynamic imports to reduce static dependency graphs and improve tree-shaking, while strictly adhering to the PascalCase directory hierarchy.\n\n**SideCar Changes**: Synchronize to the latest commit to align the native backend with the updated frontend event relays and ensure binary compatibility.\n\nThese changes continue the strategic decomposition of the UI workbench, enabling finer-grained maintenance and cleaner separation of concerns between the Mountain backend and Sky frontend.",
			"SHA": "ab9a007eccbce426598b8822959bfe09818d7c1d"
		}
	],
